,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1223.253079958,"data":"  [battery  803.8s]   batch   1024  clean     0.011 ms  faithful     0.011 ms  faithful/clean  0.977  clean/ref    0.04  faithful/ref    0.04  same obs True\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1223.2537966,"data":"  [battery  803.8s]   batch   2048  clean     0.011 ms  faithful     0.011 ms  faithful/clean  0.961  clean/ref    0.02  faithful/ref    0.02  same obs True\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1223.254509905,"data":"  [battery  803.8s] \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1223.255226912,"data":"  [battery  803.8s] ==============================================================================\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1223.255958621,"data":"  [battery  803.8s]   5. what this does NOT say\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1223.256734934,"data":"  [battery  803.8s] ==============================================================================\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1223.257458468,"data":"  [battery  803.8s]   * No whole-step number is a denominator anywhere above. The\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1223.258224838,"data":"  [battery  803.8s]     reference's whole step is printed as CONTEXT only: it is 7\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1223.258935038,"data":"  [battery  803.8s]     launches, five of them state updates.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1223.25964165,"data":"  [battery  803.8s]   * The ratio against the reference is render-against-render, both\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1223.260340516,"data":"  [battery  803.8s]     producing the same uint8 observation at the same batch on the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1223.261004135,"data":"  [battery  803.8s]     same card. If the digests differ, the ratio is between two\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1223.261670193,"data":"  [battery  803.8s]     different computations.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1223.262400649,"data":"  [battery  803.8s]   * The clean-vs-faithful delta is the crossing cost. It is the only\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1223.263108232,"data":"  [battery  803.8s]     number here that no other arm in this study has.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1223.263812457,"data":"  [battery  803.8s] \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1223.264515047,"data":"  [battery  803.8s] wrote /kaggle/working/faithful_battery.json\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.430500106,"data":"  [battery] exit 0 after 806.0s\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.431742803,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.43240265,"data":"--- 8. the three-way table, and the clean-vs-faithful delta ---\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.433927431,"data":"   batch      ref us    clean ms    faith ms   f/clean  clean/ref  faith/ref   kernels c/f  same obs\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.4355054,"data":"     512       159.0       0.012       0.011     0.908       0.08       0.07         42/42  True\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.436378862,"data":"    1024       297.0       0.011       0.011     0.977       0.04       0.04         10/10  True\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.437320422,"data":"    2048       571.4       0.011       0.011     0.961       0.02       0.02         10/10  True\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.438349942,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.439625288,"data":"--- what these numbers are, and are not ---\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.440649584,"data":"  * The three columns are RENDERS. Same world, same cameras, same\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.441720123,"data":"    max_steps, same uint8 observation, same card, same run, equal batch.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.442811083,"data":"    `f/clean` is the crossing cost and is the number this arm adds; the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.443637148,"data":"    two `*/ref` columns are render-against-render and are the same\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.444664563,"data":"    comparison `notes/19` §5.2 makes.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.445571416,"data":"  * The reference's whole-step figure is printed for context and is NOT a\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.446437415,"data":"    denominator anywhere. `4.55 M env-steps/s` covers 7 launches.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.447359242,"data":"  * `same obs` compares the two modes' observations by sha256. Both are\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.448074504,"data":"    verified against the same float64 transcription and the same naive\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.449461684,"data":"    port, so a False here would mean the crossings changed the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.450376977,"data":"    computation, and the ratios above it would be between two different\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.451601419,"data":"    computations.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.452396804,"data":"  * The ratio to the reference is NOT attributed to the compiler unless\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.453331631,"data":"    both sides did the same work. Each mode's mean steps/pixel is in the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.454467385,"data":"    battery output. The reference's own DEVICE-side step count is NOT\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.455543416,"data":"    available here: it needs the dda_probe_kernel from\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.456646055,"data":"    minecu_ref/bench/bench.cu, which refdrv.cu does not link, and putting\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.457716093,"data":"    the CPU model's number under the same label would be a claim about a\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.458804276,"data":"    device that was not measured. The workload check is one-sided and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.459865449,"data":"    the note says so rather than rounding it up.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.460977531,"data":"  * The obs_sha256 in the battery is this port's. verify.py proved it\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.462102991,"data":"    equals the naive port's and a float64 transcription's ON THIS CARD in\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.463239232,"data":"    this run. It is NOT compared against the reference's dumped bytes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.464377081,"data":"    here; that is notes/19's comparison on the reference's own state, and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.465815747,"data":"    this arm did not re-derive it.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.466878088,"data":"  * No SASS number is reported here. The instruction and register counts\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.467831308,"data":"    come from the offline archlab route on the host, where ptxas and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.468865819,"data":"    cuobjdump exist and nvcc's version is pinned; the T4 image's CUDA\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.470276962,"data":"    version is recorded but not used for a count.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":1225.47109654,"data":"\n"}
